      en: "Tibnin Castle (Toron) is located in the highlands of southern Lebanon, about 20 kilometers east of Tyre. Built in 1104 by Crusaders, it was a key fortress of the Lordship of Toron. The castle controlled the road between Tyre and Damascus. It consists of a citadel with a square keep and massive walls. In the 12th century, it was captured by the Ayyubids and later administered by the Mamluks. The site is now an archaeological site, partly ruined but still impressive. The castle stands on a hill at 500 meters elevation.",
