      en: "Gibelacar Castle (also Giblet or Byblos Castle) is located in the town of Byblos (Jbeil). It is one of the oldest and best-preserved Crusader castles in Lebanon. Built in the 12th century, it reused Roman and Phoenician foundations. The castle has a square plan with four towers and a central courtyard. It served as a residence and defensive structure. In the 13th century, it was captured and reinforced by the Mamluks. Today, the castle houses a museum and is part of the UNESCO World Heritage site of Byblos. Annual visitors exceed 200,000.",
