      en: "Enfeh Ancient Ruins, located 15 km north of Tripoli on a rocky peninsula, reveal a multi-layered history from Neolithic times through the Crusader period. The site was a key Phoenician and Roman quarry, supplying stone for temples and public buildings. A Crusader castle with cisterns and walls was built atop earlier remains. The coastal location fostered trade in purple dye and glass. Excavations have uncovered rock-cut tombs, olive presses, and Byzantine churches. The unique geology of sandstone cliffs and sea caves adds to the site's significance.",
