      en: "The Gibran Museum in Bcharre is dedicated to the Lebanese-American writer and painter Kahlil Gibran. It is housed in a 17th-century monastery that was once Gibran's intended final resting place. The museum displays his original paintings, manuscripts, personal belongings, and furniture. A recreation of his studio is included. Opened in 1995, the museum offers insight into Gibran's philosophical and artistic legacy. The surrounding cedar forests and mountains inspired much of his work. It is a significant cultural site in Lebanon.",
